text.section:
Every application for an escort vehicle driver certificate shall be made on a form prescribed by the Department, and the applicant shall write his usual signature in ink in the space provided on the form. A person who applies for an escort vehicle driver certificate must meet the following requirements:

Be at least 18 years of age;


Hold a valid Virginia driver's license or a valid driver's license for another state;


Authorize the Department to review his driving record;


Present satisfactory proof of successful completion of an eight-hour escort vehicle driver certification training course, as required by § 46.2-2904;


Pass the escort vehicle driver certification knowledge test as required by § 46.2-2905 with a score of 80 percent or higher; and


Pay the appropriate fee for certificate issuance.
